diff --git a/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-msm8226/README.cpu-runtime b/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-msm8226/README.cpu-runtime
deleted file mode 100644
index c41d64aa8..000000000
--- a/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-msm8226/README.cpu-runtime
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,18 +0,0 @@
-Development source-build candidate, not a qualified device release.
-
-Pinned Linux base 4b800b920c7db82e8012a580a17cc2d8ff9d5e66 plus the 39
-ordered patches recorded in source-provenance.json reconstruct the complete
-runtime clock-guard candidate. The exact host-tested configuration gives
-6.18.59-fx0-cpr-runtime and keeps cpufreq-dt modular. Signing keys and proprietary
-firmware/calibration are absent from this recipe.
-
-The ordinary Fx0 DTB passed one moduleless L2/S2 RAM bootstrap and timed return.
-The separate qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dtb has not booted. It explicitly selects
-the experimental calibration/domain/clock-normalization path. Do not select it
-for an unattended installed policy: schedutil could immediately request higher
-eligible rates. CPR, DVFS, analog rails, thermal, suspend, shared-SoC regression
-and update/recovery acceptance remain open. The earlier r51 EDL cause remains
-unresolved, so first controller trials remain RAM-only.
-
-Package build and host checks are separate from hardware acceptance. No
-installation or persistent boot-partition change is authorized by this file.
